\section{Finite-Step Regional Capture of the Live MEKF}
\label{sec:finite-live-capture}

The block-local result of Sec.~\ref{sec:iss-block-basin} establishes local ISS
of the normal Live recursion from its analytical structure.  Startup requires a
different statement because the initialized filter can begin farther from the
equilibrium and can undergo a bounded covariance/OU settling transient.  The
operational result below is therefore formulated directly for the complete
implemented nonlinear Live map.  A structured post-handoff set is propagated
by verified finite-step comparison envelopes until it reaches a smaller robustly
invariant regional set.  Individual samples and individual lifted intervals are
not required to contract.

\subsection{Structured regional coordinates and exact lifted map}

Use the sensitive/kinematic split of
Eqs.~\eqref{eq:iss-block-xi}--\eqref{eq:iss-block-ell},
\begin{equation}
 \vct e=(\vct e_\xi,\vct e_\ell),
 \qquad
 \vct e_\xi=(\delta\vct\theta,\delta\vct b_g,
              \delta\vct S,\delta\vct a_w,\delta\vct b_a),
 \qquad
 \vct e_\ell=(\delta\vct v,\delta\vct p).
\end{equation}
Let $\pi_k$ denote the complete normal-Live proof mode at sample $k$, including
the implemented covariance, enabled-state flags, staged OU/$R_S$ parameters,
and accepted-update pattern.  On the declared compact regional mode family,
choose uniformly positive-definite block metrics
$\mat Q_\xi(\pi)$ and $\mat Q_\ell(\pi)$ and define
\begin{align}
 r_{\xi,k}(\vct e)
 &:=\bigl(\vct e_\xi^\top\mat Q_\xi(\pi_k)\vct e_\xi\bigr)^{1/2},\\
 r_{\ell,k}(\vct e)
 &:=\bigl(\vct e_\ell^\top\mat Q_\ell(\pi_k)\vct e_\ell\bigr)^{1/2},\\
 \vct r_k(\vct e)&:=(r_{\xi,k},r_{\ell,k})^\top .
 \label{eq:capture-structured-radii}
\end{align}
A fixed dimensionless metric or a mode-dependent metric derived from the
implemented covariance may be used, provided the chosen family is uniformly
positive definite.  The two-block construction avoids forcing attitude,
$S$, bias, velocity, and position errors into one spherical radius.

For a lift of $m\ge1$ samples, denote the complete implemented nonlinear error
map by
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 \vct e_{k+m}
 =\mathcal F_{k,m}
   (\vct e_k,\vct d_{k:k+m-1};\pi_{k:k+m}).}
 \label{eq:capture-exact-lift}
\end{equation}
The map contains the exact prediction, executed accelerometer and magnetometer
corrections, the full $S=0$ Kalman correction, quaternion injection/reset,
covariance propagation, state-enable staging, and predictable adaptive
schedule.  In particular, the $S=0$ correction retains its attitude and bias
rows through cross-covariance.  No Schmidt, block-only, or gain-truncated
approximation is introduced.

For $\vct a\in\mathbb R_+^2$, define
\begin{equation}
 \mathcal C_k(\vct a)
 :=\{\vct e:\vct r_k(\vct e)\preceq\vct a\},
 \label{eq:capture-structured-box}
\end{equation}
where vector inequalities are componentwise.  Choose positive vectors
\begin{equation}
 0\prec\vct R_B\prec\vct R_C\preceq\vct R_D .
 \label{eq:capture-region-order}
\end{equation}
Here $\mathcal C_k(\vct R_D)$ is the chart- and measurement-safe proof domain,
$\mathcal C_k(\vct R_C)$ is the outer handoff/capture set, and
$\mathcal B_k:=\mathcal C_k(\vct R_B)$ is the inner regional set.  A trajectory
may temporarily leave $\mathcal C_k(\vct R_C)$ during capture, provided every
verified prefix remains inside $\mathcal C_k(\vct R_D)$.

\subsection{Exact comparison envelopes}

For a deterministic disturbance budget
$\|\vct d\|_\infty\le\overline d$, define the componentwise envelope of the
complete lift by
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 [\mathcal T_{k,m}(\vct a;\overline d)]_i
 :=\sup
 \left\{
 r_{i,k+m}\!\left(
 \mathcal F_{k,m}(\vct e,\vct d;\pi)
 \right):
 \vct e\in\mathcal C_k(\vct a),
 \ \|\vct d\|_\infty\le\overline d,
 \ \pi\in\Pi_{k,m}
 \right\},}
 \quad i\in\{\xi,\ell\}.
 \label{eq:capture-comparison-envelope}
\end{equation}
The admissible family $\Pi_{k,m}$ contains only predictable schedules and
accepted-update patterns satisfying the declared Live assumptions.  Compactness
of the certified domain and continuity of the implemented local error map make
the suprema finite.  Since
$\mathcal C_k(\vct a)\subseteq\mathcal C_k(\vct b)$ whenever
$\vct a\preceq\vct b$, the envelope is monotone:
\begin{equation}
 \vct a\preceq\vct b
 \quad\Longrightarrow\quad
 \mathcal T_{k,m}(\vct a;\overline d)
 \preceq
 \mathcal T_{k,m}(\vct b;\overline d).
 \label{eq:capture-comparison-monotone}
\end{equation}
Prefix envelopes $\mathcal T_{k,j}^{\rm pre}$, $1\le j<m$, are defined by the
same supremum with $\mathcal F_{k,j}$.  Because the envelope is evaluated on the
complete nonlinear map, cancellation produced by the Kalman correction,
quaternion reset, and subsequent prediction is retained.

Choose an admissible sequence of lift lengths $m_n\ge1$, let $k_0=k_H$ and
$k_{n+1}=k_n+m_n$, and define the comparison recursion
\begin{equation}
 \overline{\vct r}_{n+1}
 =\mathcal T_{k_n,m_n}(\overline{\vct r}_n;\overline d).
 \label{eq:capture-comparison-sequence}
\end{equation}
The maps may vary with $n$.  Consequently, early post-handoff lifts may expand
while later lifts contract more strongly; no common one-step contraction factor
is assumed.

\begin{theorem}[Finite-step regional Live capture and practical ISS]
\label{thm:finite-live-capture}
Assume the exact comparison envelopes are valid on
$\mathcal C_k(\vct R_D)$.  Starting from
$\overline{\vct r}^{\,C}_0=\vct R_C$, generate
Eq.~\eqref{eq:capture-comparison-sequence}.  Suppose a finite $N_C$ exists such
that
\begin{align}
 \overline{\vct r}^{\,C}_n&\preceq\vct R_D,
 &&0\le n\le N_C,
 \label{eq:capture-lift-domain}\\
 \mathcal T^{\rm pre}_{k_n,j}
 (\overline{\vct r}^{\,C}_n;\overline d)
 &\preceq\vct R_D,
 &&0\le n<N_C,\quad1\le j<m_n,
 \label{eq:capture-prefix-domain}\\
 \overline{\vct r}^{\,C}_{N_C}&\preceq\vct R_B.
 \label{eq:capture-finite-entry}
\end{align}
Assume further that every admissible post-capture normal-Live lift has chart-safe
prefixes and satisfies
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 \mathcal T_{k,m}(\vct R_B;\overline d)\preceq\vct R_B,}
 \label{eq:capture-inner-invariance}
\end{equation}
and that for some positive weight vector $\vct w$, some
$0<\lambda_B<1$, and a class-$\mathcal K$ function $\gamma_B$,
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 \|\mathcal T_{k,m}(\vct a;\overline d)\|_{\vct w,\infty}
 \le
 \lambda_B\|\vct a\|_{\vct w,\infty}
 +\gamma_B(\overline d),
 \qquad
 0\preceq\vct a\preceq\vct R_B,}
 \label{eq:capture-inner-contraction}
\end{equation}
where
$\|\vct a\|_{\vct w,\infty}:=\max_i a_i/w_i$.
Then every deterministic Live trajectory beginning in
$\mathcal C_{k_H}(\vct R_C)$ remains in the certified proof domain, enters
$\mathcal B_{k_{N_C}}$ after at most $N_C$ lifted intervals, and remains in the
inner regional set thereafter.  For every post-capture lifted index $j$,
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 \|\vct r_{k_{N_C+j}}\|_{\vct w,\infty}
 \le
 \lambda_B^j\|\vct r_{k_{N_C}}\|_{\vct w,\infty}
 +\frac{1-\lambda_B^j}{1-\lambda_B}\gamma_B(\overline d).}
 \label{eq:capture-practical-iss}
\end{equation}
Thus the full nonlinear Live recursion is regionally practically ISS on the
captured set.  If $\overline d=0$, the captured error converges exponentially to
zero.
\end{theorem}

\begin{proof}
Let
$\vct r_{k_H}(\vct e_{k_H})\preceq\vct R_C
=\overline{\vct r}^{\,C}_0$.  Monotonicity
Eq.~\eqref{eq:capture-comparison-monotone} and the definition of the envelope
give by induction
\begin{equation}
 \vct r_{k_n}(\vct e_{k_n})
 \preceq\overline{\vct r}^{\,C}_n,
 \qquad0\le n\le N_C.
\end{equation}
The prefix inequalities Eq.~\eqref{eq:capture-prefix-domain} keep every
intermediate sample inside $\mathcal C(\vct R_D)$ even when an early prefix or
complete lift grows.  Equation~\eqref{eq:capture-finite-entry} gives
$\vct r_{k_{N_C}}\preceq\vct R_B$.  Monotonicity together with
Eq.~\eqref{eq:capture-inner-invariance} proves forward invariance of the inner
set.  Iterating Eq.~\eqref{eq:capture-inner-contraction} then gives the geometric
series in Eq.~\eqref{eq:capture-practical-iss}.
\end{proof}

The result is a finite-step Lyapunov/comparison theorem.  A composite sequence
$\mathcal T_{k_{q-1},m_{q-1}}\circ\cdots\circ
 \mathcal T_{k_0,m_0}$ may map the outer set inward even if one or more
constituent lifts expand it, matching the permitted post-\texttt{goLive()}
settling transient.

\subsection{Handoff-specific capture time}

The basin-wide construction starts from the complete outer set.  Startup begins
from its own structured handoff envelope.  Let
$\vct R_H\preceq\vct R_C$ be a certified handoff bound and define
\begin{equation}
 \overline{\vct r}^{\,H}_0=\vct R_H,
 \qquad
 \overline{\vct r}^{\,H}_{n+1}
 =\mathcal T_{k_n,m_n}
  (\overline{\vct r}^{\,H}_n;\overline d).
 \label{eq:capture-handoff-sequence}
\end{equation}
The startup capture count is
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 N_H:=\min\{n\ge0:
 \overline{\vct r}^{\,H}_n\preceq\vct R_B\}.}
 \label{eq:capture-count}
\end{equation}
Whenever the outer-set certificate exists, monotonicity gives $N_H\le N_C$.
The corresponding time bounds are
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 T_H\le h_{\max}\sum_{n=0}^{N_H-1}m_n,
 \qquad
 T_C\le h_{\max}\sum_{n=0}^{N_C-1}m_n.}
 \label{eq:capture-time}
\end{equation}
Thus the certified startup time is computed from the actual admissible handoff
family rather than from the boundary of the larger outer set.

\subsection{Operational capture-certificate contract}
\label{sec:capture-certificate-contract}

The numerical certificate starts from the covariance and estimator mode
produced by the actual \texttt{goLive()} handoff, including staged OU
parameters, covariance synchronization, the enabled linear block, the full
$S=0$ gain, and the initially held accelerometer-bias update.  No artificial
pre-capture covariance warm-up is permitted.

Let $\vct R_H$ be the structured worst-case handoff radius supplied by
Sec.~\ref{sec:semiglobal-handoff}.  Define the dimensionless handoff margin
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 \eta_H:=
 \min_{i\in\{\xi,\ell\}}
 \left(1-\frac{R_{H,i}}{R_{C,i}}\right).}
 \label{eq:capture-handoff-margin}
\end{equation}
The certificate reports at least
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 \{\vct R_H,\vct R_B,\vct R_C,\vct R_D,
   \eta_H,N_H,T_H,N_C,T_C,B_{\rm pre},
   \vct w,\lambda_B,\gamma_B\},}
 \label{eq:capture-certificate-outputs}
\end{equation}
where $B_{\rm pre}$ is the largest verified normalized prefix amplification and
$N_C,T_C$ may be omitted when only the declared handoff family, rather than the
whole outer set, is certified.  The startup pass conditions are
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 \vct R_H\prec\vct R_C\preceq\vct R_D,
 \qquad
 \overline{\vct r}^{\,H}_{N_H}\preceq\vct R_B,
 \qquad
 N_H<\infty,
 \qquad
 \lambda_B<1,}
 \label{eq:capture-certificate-pass}
\end{equation}
together with the prefix-domain and inner-invariance conditions
Eqs.~\eqref{eq:capture-prefix-domain} and
\eqref{eq:capture-inner-invariance}.

\subsection{Stochastic Live qualification}
\label{sec:capture-stochastic}

The deterministic capture theorem uses $\overline d$ only for perturbations that
are legitimately bounded on the declared capture interval, such as bounded
model mismatch.  Gaussian process and measurement noise are treated separately
because their infinite-horizon sample supremum is not bounded by a fixed
deterministic constant.

\begin{theorem}[Mean-square practical stability under stochastic Live noise]
\label{thm:capture-stochastic-live}
Let $\mathscr F_n$ be the filtration at the post-capture lifted indices and let
$V_n\ge0$ be uniformly equivalent to the squared structured norm: for constants
$0<a_1\le a_2<\infty$,
\begin{equation}
 a_1\|\vct r_n\|_{\vct w,\infty}^2
 \le V_n\le
 a_2\|\vct r_n\|_{\vct w,\infty}^2.
 \label{eq:capture-stochastic-equivalence}
\end{equation}
Suppose that, for every lifted index on the horizon under consideration, the
exact stochastic Live map satisfies almost surely
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 \mathbb E[V_{n+1}\mid\mathscr F_n]
 \le\lambda_sV_n+\sigma_s^2,
 \qquad 0<\lambda_s<1.}
 \label{eq:capture-stochastic-drift}
\end{equation}
If this condition holds for all $n\ge0$, then
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 \mathbb E[V_n]
 \le
 \lambda_s^n\mathbb E[V_0]
 +\frac{1-\lambda_s^n}{1-\lambda_s}\sigma_s^2,}
 \label{eq:capture-stochastic-ms}
\end{equation}
and consequently
\begin{equation}
 \mathbb E\|\vct r_n\|_{\vct w,\infty}^2
 \le\frac{1}{a_1}
 \left(
 \lambda_s^n\mathbb E[V_0]
 +\frac{\sigma_s^2}{1-\lambda_s}
 \right).
 \label{eq:capture-stochastic-state-ms}
\end{equation}
For every $A>0$,
\begin{equation}
 \Pr\{V_n\ge A\}
 \le\frac{1}{A}
 \left(
 \lambda_s^n\mathbb E[V_0]
 +\frac{1-\lambda_s^n}{1-\lambda_s}\sigma_s^2
 \right),
 \label{eq:capture-stochastic-one-time}
\end{equation}
and, over any finite horizon $0\le n\le N$ on which
Eq.~\eqref{eq:capture-stochastic-drift} is valid,
\begin{equation}
 \Pr\left\{\max_{0\le j\le N}V_j\ge A\right\}
 \le\frac{1}{A}\sum_{j=0}^{N}
 \left(
 \lambda_s^j\mathbb E[V_0]
 +\frac{1-\lambda_s^j}{1-\lambda_s}\sigma_s^2
 \right).
 \label{eq:capture-stochastic-finite-hp}
\end{equation}
\end{theorem}

\begin{proof}
Taking total expectation in Eq.~\eqref{eq:capture-stochastic-drift} and
iterating the scalar affine recursion gives
Eq.~\eqref{eq:capture-stochastic-ms}.  The lower norm-equivalence inequality
gives Eq.~\eqref{eq:capture-stochastic-state-ms}.  Markov's inequality gives
Eq.~\eqref{eq:capture-stochastic-one-time}; applying it for each
$j=0,\ldots,N$ and using the union bound gives
Eq.~\eqref{eq:capture-stochastic-finite-hp}.
\end{proof}

The stochastic statement does not assert almost-sure invariance of a finite
local chart under unbounded Gaussian support.  Its infinite-horizon mean-square
conclusion requires Eq.~\eqref{eq:capture-stochastic-drift} for every lifted
index.  When the drift inequality is certified only on a finite stochastic
domain or horizon, only the corresponding finite-horizon bounds are claimed.
